 "assumptions": {
  "SIM_TORSO": [
   "A crown-kit setting between the simulated torsos (15 / 19 / 23 in) takes the bag forces of the nearest simulated torso (17.5, 18, 20, 20.5 -> 19 in); the other neighbour is run as a check and the worse of the two is reported. The crown (legs, bushings, top bar) is the kit's own at the setting's torso.",
   "A CORRIE F fine meat run at 18 and 20.5 in (corrie_f_sim.py finerun F --torso 18 / 20.5)."
  ],
  "SIM_BODY": [
   "As BL-021 (im3_body_simloads ASSUMPTION SIM_BODY): the sim's 1 g frame-side forces scaled by g x load / 68 kg, closed on the payload weight at the sim CG.",
   "T9 loaded CG + frame strain gauges at the stays and the lumbar struts in the T1 carry test."
  ],
  "CINCH_STATIC": [
   "As BL-021: the meat-strap cinch is a static preload, in every strength and creep set but not in the static-carry set that gives fatigue; the cycled bound is reported beside it.",
   "MT-1 strap tension readout over a 10 min loaded walk in the T2 meat test."
  ],
  "PAHT_FAT": [
   "PAHT-CF fatigue_1e5_ratio 0.30 (record ASSUMPTION).",
   "CA-1 coupon test (flip point in section 6)."
  ],
  "FI99": [
   "The body margin is H1's FI99 rule (99th percentile of the failure index over the non-load-patch voxels, 2 mm grid, frame_comp_d.evaluate). A change that adds material is credited only through the stresses it lowers; the governing region's own percentile is reported beside it so the body number is not raised by diluting the population.",
   "T1 frame strain gauges at the lumbar struts / stay feet (z 100-200) against the voxel model's strain."
  ],
  "LINER": [
   "Sleeve liner trial: a bonded tube in the bore is modelled as the bore ring r 9-11 mm with its Young's modulus scaled so the ring's bending stiffness EI equals the tube's (6061-T6 20 x 1 mm; voxel ring I from the 2 mm grid). Bond assumed perfect; the liner's own stress is not part of the body FI.",
   "Only needed if a liner is adopted: a bonded-liner coupon (push-out) and a stay 3-point bend."
  ],
  "LEG_ENGAGE": [
   "Longer-leg trial: each kit's legs are lengthened so that at the kit's lowest setting the leg bottom sits at H1's 15 in depth (z 171): +127 mm each (crown_diet deepest leg bottom z 298).",
   "Only needed if adopted: crown legs FPF re-run (crown_diet.crown_margins) at the new length."
  ]
 },
